@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy";
}

<div class="page">
    <div class="container" style="max-width:820px">
        <div class="page-header">
            <h1>Privacy and data handling</h1>
            <p>How Elevate Workforce Solution stores and uses the information you give us.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="prose-block">
            <h3>What we store</h3>
            <p>
                We store the details you enter on your profile: your name, email address, phone number,
                location, professional title, work history, education, skills, certifications and languages.
                Employers store a company profile and the vacancies they post.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="prose-block">
            <h3>Your resume</h3>
            <p>
                Resumes are stored outside the public web folder under a generated file name, so they can
                never be reached by guessing a URL. Access is checked on every request: you can read your
                own resumes, and an employer can read a resume only for a candidate who applied to one of
                their vacancies. An administrator can read any resume in order to moderate the platform.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="prose-block">
            <h3>Who can see your profile</h3>
            <p>
                Employers browsing an applicant see the candidate details attached to that application.
                Your contact details are not published on any public page.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="prose-block">
            <h3>The match score</h3>
            <p>
                The compatibility score shown on a vacancy is calculated by comparing the keywords, experience
                and location on your profile with the requirements of the vacancy. It is produced by rules in
                this application, it is informational only, and it is never used to automatically reject or
                hire anyone.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="prose-block">
            <h3>Your choices</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>Edit or remove anything on your profile at any time.</li>
                <li>Withdraw an application while the employer has not made a decision.</li>
                <li>Ask an administrator to deactivate your account.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="prose-block">
            <h3>Contact</h3>
            <p>
                For any question about your data, sign in and use the account settings page, or ask your
                employer contact to raise it with the platform administrator.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
